Who's that? Who is that?

00:54:30.700 --> 00:54:31.100
Now?

00:54:33.910 --> 00:54:38.100
Scat, Scat, get out of the darn those cats anyway.

00:54:40.670 --> 00:54:41.890
Betty, then you will come with me.

00:54:42.730 --> 00:54:43.790
Steve, I don't...

00:54:44.450 --> 00:54:46.350
Please, Betty, please.

00:54:47.050 --> 00:54:48.350
All right, I will.

00:54:48.760 --> 00:54:49.900
Oh, that makes me so happy.

00:54:50.160 --> 00:54:52.400
Betty, go and pack your bag and I'll be back in a jiffy.

00:54:53.590 --> 00:54:53.870
Hurry.

00:54:57.380 --> 00:54:57.840
What was it?

00:54:58.420 --> 00:54:59.960
Oh, just a lot of darn cats.

00:55:09.900 --> 00:55:10.560
There, dear?

00:55:11.190 --> 00:55:11.510
Yes.

00:55:11.940 --> 00:55:12.500
Are you all ready?

00:55:13.290 --> 00:55:16.920
Yes, but how am I to know you really love me?

00:55:17.040 --> 00:55:18.420
Oh, how can you doubt me?

00:55:44.840 --> 00:55:46.620
Is there anybody down there?

00:55:48.190 --> 00:55:49.290
I beg your pardon.

00:55:49.860 --> 00:55:51.340
I thought I heard someone.

00:56:02.460 --> 00:56:03.580
Here we are, Steve, dear.

00:56:07.600 --> 00:56:08.580
It's evening, isn't it?

00:56:08.990 --> 00:56:10.050
You go away from here this minute.

00:56:10.310 --> 00:56:12.190
I'm not going away from here, and neither are you.

00:56:12.290 --> 00:56:13.070
Oh, I hate you.

00:56:13.320 --> 00:56:14.380
Well, that's better than nothing.

00:56:14.720 --> 00:56:16.660
What right have you got to mix up in my affairs, anyway?

00:56:17.070 --> 00:56:19.590
I came here to thrill you, and I'm going to do it.

00:56:19.670 --> 00:56:21.440
Oh, you leave me go this minute, or I'll scream.

00:56:21.580 --> 00:56:22.160
Go ahead and scream.

00:56:24.480 --> 00:56:25.420
What was that?

00:56:25.720 --> 00:56:27.260
Oh, I don't know.

00:56:28.400 --> 00:56:29.100
Come in, May.

00:56:33.000 --> 00:56:34.110
Wait for me, Peter.

00:56:38.730 --> 00:56:40.050
Who's that screaming down there?

00:56:40.280 --> 00:56:41.740
Sounds like a murder.

00:56:42.240 --> 00:56:44.300
This is the goofiest place I ever lived in.

00:56:44.560 --> 00:56:46.220
Well, I'll find out who it is.

00:56:46.460 --> 00:56:47.810
Be careful, Peter.

00:56:48.980 --> 00:56:50.080
Treat me this way.

00:56:54.730 --> 00:56:55.070
Hurry.

00:57:02.750 --> 00:57:03.840
Betty! Betty! Betty!

00:57:04.860 --> 00:57:07.300
Are you all right, dear?

00:57:07.770 --> 00:57:09.210
No, I'm all right.

00:57:26.910 --> 00:57:27.910
What's the matter with you?

00:57:28.230 --> 00:57:29.070
Nothing, sir.

00:57:30.060 --> 00:57:31.400
I never saw such a night.

00:57:32.550 --> 00:57:32.910
Willie.

00:57:33.350 --> 00:57:33.750
Yes, sir.

00:57:33.830 --> 00:57:35.650
What do you suppose that screaming was?

00:57:35.870 --> 00:57:36.870
I don't know, sir.

00:57:37.130 --> 00:57:38.030
Well, why don't you?

00:57:38.210 --> 00:57:39.650
Oh, I don't know that either, sir.

00:57:40.210 --> 00:57:41.550
Let's go around the side of the house.

00:57:41.710 --> 00:57:44.390
If I find them, I'll blow their brains out.

00:57:44.470 --> 00:57:44.970
No, sir.

00:57:45.190 --> 00:57:45.470
What?

00:57:45.810 --> 00:57:46.470
Yes, sir.

00:57:46.590 --> 00:57:47.150
Well, come on.

00:58:38.060 --> 00:58:38.760
Morning, Mary Jane.

00:58:39.120 --> 00:58:41.100
What brings you around here before breakfast?

00:58:41.440 --> 00:58:42.000
Your father.

00:58:42.220 --> 00:58:42.820
My father?

00:58:43.640 --> 00:58:45.280
He never invited you for breakfast.

00:58:45.680 --> 00:58:46.520
Oh, I know it.

00:58:46.770 --> 00:58:48.930
But the only chance you get to say anything around here

00:58:48.930 --> 00:58:51.710
is either after he goes to bed or before he gets up in the morning.

00:58:51.970 --> 00:58:52.350
Uh-uh.

00:58:52.590 --> 00:58:54.170
That sounds like a dirty crack.

00:58:54.440 --> 00:58:54.940
That was.

00:58:55.120 --> 00:58:57.390
Say, what do you want around here anyway?

00:58:58.850 --> 00:58:59.770
I want you.

00:59:01.210 --> 00:59:06.580
I'm sick and tired of having you around, all around me.

00:59:07.700 --> 00:59:11.960
Say, most everywhere I go, you're there to hound me.

00:59:12.760 --> 00:59:15.630
And how you love to hound me away.

00:59:17.000 --> 00:59:20.120
There's something that I want to ask of you.

00:59:22.390 --> 00:59:24.760
Do any you ask to.

00:59:26.780 --> 00:59:28.320
Raise your head up higher.

00:59:29.310 --> 00:59:29.910
Put your two.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:39.370
lips here make me feel on fire say what's the big idea oh with that big moon blazing just for

00:59:39.370 --> 00:59:49.140
atmosphere i get so darn brazen say what's the big idea just start the party smarty and i'll produce

00:59:49.140 --> 00:59:58.840
i don't mean maybe baby i'm on the loose oh i'm so wild and woolly like a texas deer

01:00:00.220 --> 01:00:01.380
Isn't that just a bully?

01:00:02.230 --> 01:00:03.570
What's the big idea?

01:00:03.930 --> 01:00:05.750
What's your proposition?

01:00:06.950 --> 01:00:08.370
Buzz it in my ear

01:00:09.200 --> 01:00:10.600
Use your intuition

01:00:10.600 --> 01:00:12.890
Hey, what's the big idea?

01:00:13.570 --> 01:00:15.080
What's your occupation?

01:00:16.260 --> 01:00:17.300
I'm an engineer

01:00:17.300 --> 01:00:20.110
You just passed your station

01:00:20.110 --> 01:00:22.150
What's the big idea?

01:00:23.340 --> 01:00:26.700
You're engineering something without a plan

01:00:26.700 --> 01:00:29.710
The way you use your hands

01:00:31.530 --> 01:00:33.830
Oh, get a reputation.

01:00:34.760 --> 01:00:36.080
Don't you anchor here?

01:00:37.340 --> 01:00:38.600
Take a long vacation.

01:00:39.410 --> 01:00:40.870
Hey, what's a big idea?

01:00:41.410 --> 01:00:41.510
Huh?

01:01:36.270 --> 01:01:37.310
Good morning, Henry.

01:01:37.510 --> 01:01:38.490
Good morning, Peter.

01:01:38.860 --> 01:01:39.700
Is Betty down yet?

01:01:39.960 --> 01:01:40.600
No, Peter.

01:01:40.960 --> 01:01:41.080
Hmm.

01:01:41.780 --> 01:01:44.460
Well, this is one morning she didn't stay out until five o'clock.

01:01:44.620 --> 01:01:50.250
You here again?

01:01:50.780 --> 01:01:51.620
Morning, Mr. Braley.

01:01:51.820 --> 01:01:51.960
Morning.

01:01:52.220 --> 01:01:52.960
Going duck shooting?

01:01:53.180 --> 01:01:55.420
No, I'm hunting, uh, ukulele players.

01:01:55.640 --> 01:01:57.540
Please don't shoot again until you've read this.

01:01:58.360 --> 01:01:58.860
What's this?

01:01:59.180 --> 01:01:59.880
A letter of introduction.

01:02:00.730 --> 01:02:11.650
Emily, I regret to inform you that your Scotch terrier Lassie has the rickets.

01:02:12.500 --> 01:02:15.880
Young man, if this is a joke, there's one person in this room that won't laugh.

01:02:16.240 --> 01:02:18.280
Sorry, Mr. Braley. I gave you the wrong letter.

01:02:18.400 --> 01:02:19.080
I thought so.

01:02:19.420 --> 01:02:28.200
You're not George Alden's son.

01:02:28.880 --> 01:02:29.180
Les?

01:02:29.420 --> 01:02:29.740
No!

01:02:30.090 --> 01:02:36.380
yes well my boy why didn't you say so why didn't you tell me last night you didn't give me a chance

01:02:36.380 --> 01:02:42.700
my gracious emily this is george halton's son my old partner up in san francisco the millionaire

01:02:42.700 --> 01:02:48.440
millionaire worse than that why a million dollars is just like car fare to george my boy i'm glad

01:02:48.440 --> 01:02:53.790
to see you what can i do for you nothing much i want to marry your daughter betty certainly

01:02:53.790 --> 01:02:58.900
nothing simpler but what's the big rush well i just got a wire from dad telling me to return

01:02:58.900 --> 01:02:59.840
and just got a knife.

01:03:00.120 --> 01:03:01.200
I want to take her with me.

01:03:01.400 --> 01:03:02.220
Surest thing you know.

01:03:02.440 --> 01:03:03.260
You can take both of them.

01:03:03.640 --> 01:03:06.680
Peter, haven't you better ask Betty first?

01:03:06.940 --> 01:03:08.240
No, we'll ask her afterwards.

01:03:08.800 --> 01:03:09.920
Say, who's running this house anyway?

01:03:10.410 --> 01:03:12.410
Mr. Braley, I'm a little pressed for time.

01:03:12.760 --> 01:03:14.240
Suppose I go and get the minister now.

01:03:14.400 --> 01:03:15.180
That's a great idea.

01:03:15.520 --> 01:03:17.540
You get the minister, and I'll get the bride.

01:03:18.360 --> 01:03:19.620
I'll be back in a nitty-gritty.

01:03:19.760 --> 01:03:20.240
Hurry up!

01:03:21.040 --> 01:03:22.820
My gracious George Alden's son.

01:03:23.290 --> 01:03:25.850
You know, there was always something about that young man that I liked.

01:03:26.290 --> 01:03:27.030
Was it, Peter?

01:03:27.290 --> 01:03:27.970
A millionaire.

01:03:28.730 --> 01:03:29.710
Well, well, well.

01:03:34.500 --> 01:03:39.930
Betty, come out, dear. This is a big day for you, and for me.

01:03:44.520 --> 01:03:45.260
Good morning, Father.

01:03:45.400 --> 01:03:47.600
Good morning, dear. I have the biggest news for you, Betty.

01:03:47.920 --> 01:03:50.260
Good morning, Mr. Braley.

01:03:51.400 --> 01:03:52.900
What are you doing in my daughter's room?

01:03:53.210 --> 01:03:55.620
Well, now, Mr. Braley, really, there's something...

01:03:55.620 --> 01:03:58.840
I should say they are. How long have you been in there?

01:03:59.090 --> 01:03:59.970
Really, sir, I was...

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.620
I'm so interested in other things that I fail to note the time.

01:04:04.270 --> 01:04:04.650
Ready?

01:04:05.010 --> 01:04:05.770
Yes, dear.

01:04:05.930 --> 01:04:06.670
Get down to breakfast.

01:04:06.870 --> 01:04:08.030
Oh, yes, Terry, dear.

01:04:25.710 --> 01:04:26.750
Where's my gun?

01:04:39.880 --> 01:04:40.540
Here we are.

01:04:40.700 --> 01:04:41.440
Good morning, Mr. Brady.

01:04:41.560 --> 01:04:41.940
Good morning.

01:04:42.380 --> 01:04:44.400
You've just arrived in time, I hope.

01:04:44.780 --> 01:04:45.740
Let's get this thing over.

01:04:45.860 --> 01:04:47.200
Listen, I don't seem to understand.

01:04:51.130 --> 01:04:52.550
Now, Dominic, do your stuff.

01:04:52.690 --> 01:04:56.170
But I fail to comprehend just what is required of me.

01:04:56.400 --> 01:04:57.240
What is required?

01:04:58.220 --> 01:04:59.740
I want you to marry my daughter.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.760
Well, I'd like to, but I can't keep on marrying the girl.

01:05:03.230 --> 01:05:03.910
What do you mean?

01:05:04.170 --> 01:05:07.190
Well, I mean that I married the young lady early this morning.

01:05:08.300 --> 01:05:10.140
What are you trying to do, marry my daughter twice?

01:05:10.420 --> 01:05:11.280
I didn't marry her.

01:05:11.630 --> 01:05:12.410
Well, who did?

01:05:12.820 --> 01:05:13.420
I did.

01:05:14.370 --> 01:05:14.870
What, you?

01:05:15.360 --> 01:05:15.800
Yes.

01:05:16.280 --> 01:05:17.860
Oh, yes.

01:05:19.070 --> 01:05:20.230
This is the bridegroom.

01:05:20.390 --> 01:05:20.990
You mean to say that?

01:05:20.990 --> 01:05:22.010
Betty, you promised.

01:05:22.710 --> 01:05:24.530
Oh, Steve, I didn't really promise.

01:05:24.770 --> 01:05:27.830
I just realized before it was too late that Terry was the one.

01:05:28.050 --> 01:05:29.640
Betty, sit down and be quiet.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:30.980
Yes, Terry, dear.

01:05:32.600 --> 01:05:34.140
But who's responsible for this?

01:05:35.450 --> 01:05:36.230
I was.

01:05:36.550 --> 01:05:38.190
Oh, so it was you, hmm?

01:05:38.450 --> 01:05:39.030
Yes, me.

01:05:39.480 --> 01:05:41.540
We all got tired of the way you've acted,

01:05:41.580 --> 01:05:44.040
and so when Terry and Betty confided in me

01:05:44.040 --> 01:05:44.960
they wanted to be married,

01:05:45.340 --> 01:05:48.270
well, we just waited until you were asleep

01:05:48.270 --> 01:05:50.550
and then quietly sneaked out.

01:05:51.430 --> 01:05:58.330
This is an awful blow to me.

01:05:59.080 --> 01:05:59.980
Oh, Steve, I...

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:00.700
I'm sorry.

01:06:00.980 --> 01:06:02.080
Sorry about what?

01:06:02.860 --> 01:06:04.200
Oh, nothing, Terry, dear.

01:06:05.280 --> 01:06:06.420
Goodbye, Mr. Alden.

01:06:12.750 --> 01:06:14.590
I imagine that, under the circumstances,

01:06:14.830 --> 01:06:17.330
my attempted officiating will be entirely superfluous.

01:06:18.000 --> 01:06:20.940
Oh, I'm sorry, Mr. Randall. I didn't know they called you.

01:06:21.380 --> 01:06:24.960
Hereafter, pay no attention to anything you're told around here,

01:06:25.390 --> 01:06:27.210
unless I okay it.

01:06:27.840 --> 01:06:29.880
Very well. Good day.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:33.730
Will you excuse me, Emily?

01:06:34.690 --> 01:06:35.760
Come, buddy.

01:06:36.600 --> 01:06:37.500
Yes, Terry, dear.

01:06:48.010 --> 01:06:50.310
Emily, I want to know what the idea of all this is.

01:06:50.310 --> 01:06:51.440
Oh, stop talking.

01:06:51.740 --> 01:06:53.580
There's been too much talk around here already.

01:06:53.920 --> 01:06:55.880
Besides, it's time you were getting down to your office.

01:06:56.610 --> 01:06:57.230
Why, Emily!

01:06:57.630 --> 01:06:57.970
Peter!

01:07:04.480 --> 01:07:10.630
Get out. That lasts you till Christmas.

01:07:15.410 --> 01:07:16.250
Do you love me, Terry?

01:07:17.760 --> 01:07:18.540
Sure I do.

01:07:19.190 --> 01:07:20.470
Do you always love me?

01:07:21.470 --> 01:07:21.870
Listen.

01:07:32.010 --> 01:07:39.490
Just a song and a story soon is a hymn to your grace.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:00.100
Thank you.

01:08:30.860 --> 01:08:31.220
Yay.
